{
    "word": "muzak",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "5ab70bb1-6878-35b5-826c-b3937ed16a94",
                "word": "Muzak",
                "pos": "name",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a8d747c1-9a4a-362a-9659-047f2cb9df97",
                        "entry_id": "5ab70bb1-6878-35b5-826c-b3937ed16a94",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Recorded background music characterized by soft, soothing instrumental sounds which is transmitted by wire, radio, or recorded media (originally on a subscription basis) to doctors' offices, shops, and other business premises."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b6ddf72d-4056-40b9-b5da-e7eedbde8a1c",
                                "sense_id": "a8d747c1-9a4a-362a-9659-047f2cb9df97",
                                "text": "It dawned on her that he was talking about the Muzak. It had been seeping in, in its subliminal, unidentifiable way since they'd entered the place, all strings, reeds, muted brass."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "497939b0-1273-490e-adb8-f210acc65df4",
                                "sense_id": "a8d747c1-9a4a-362a-9659-047f2cb9df97",
                                "text": "There's no way I can change internal body functions. Only yogis can do that. Muzak, for example, can't change you. Aaron Copeland [i.e., Aaron Copland] calls Muzak 'the obsequious.' We're super-saturated with shitty music. [Originally published in New Times.]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e8d7665d-c5e6-4456-ae4e-ba363cf72dc5",
                                "sense_id": "a8d747c1-9a4a-362a-9659-047f2cb9df97",
                                "text": "Some people, of course, have no trouble making that decision: they know they don't like Muzak. Critics charge that Muzak invades what could be pleasurable silence, disrupts conversation, or smacks of George Orwell's 1984. [Originally published in American Way.]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "431c9c0e-1ba2-4e4e-9cb9-24fd2447a05a",
                        "source_entry_id": "5ab70bb1-6878-35b5-826c-b3937ed16a94",
                        "source_sense_id": "a8d747c1-9a4a-362a-9659-047f2cb9df97",
                        "source_sense_description": "type of background music",
                        "target_lang_word": "muzak",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "muzak",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "271d1f3a-2917-3afa-9854-10bbe5745c5f",
                                        "entry_id": "93d32c75-0109-3bfb-926d-4849b65c77d1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Genre musical destiné à la diffusion comme musique d’ambiance aseptisée et normalisée dans des lieux de circulation ou sur des lignes d’attente téléphonique."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1169ddef-b58f-4515-9519-43927faf41b9",
                                                "sense_id": "271d1f3a-2917-3afa-9854-10bbe5745c5f",
                                                "text": "Kidel, par une forme de raisonnement métonymique, a décidé de réfléchir à l’un des composants de cette régulation, la muzak (justement), en ce qu’elle se caractérise par sa prédictibilité et par son utilisation dans une fonction coercitive."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2ff1c33a-b682-480a-9aba-b85b3aff42d4",
                                                "sense_id": "271d1f3a-2917-3afa-9854-10bbe5745c5f",
                                                "text": "Je l'sais qu'un jour … tu s'ras rien d'autre qu'un p'tit maudit bruit d'fond que l'on ignore comme un air de muzak."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
